IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 4 -- SUPERVISORY INFORMATION (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3206-3241 of the plain-text rendering, which is not the official
-- text and is not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR.  Regulation 51(1) (line 1715) requires a supervisory authority to collect the information it considers necessary for its supervisory functions, "including the
-- information specified in Schedule 4", and regulation 51(2) (line 1716) to provide the Treasury, on request, with such of it as the Treasury specifies.  This Schedule lists that
-- information.  Nothing in it imposes a duty on a relevant person; it means to one that the authority supervising it counts it (as a supervised person, as a firm of a given risk, as a
-- contravener) and, for suspicious activity disclosures, that a copy of what it sent the NCA may be among the information collected.  The seat questions are those.
--
-- THE ITEMS ARE UNNUMBERED IN THE RENDERING (FORK S4-F1).  The Schedule prints each item as a bare paragraph and prints no number.  They are
-- labelled here `sch 4 item N`, N being the position in the printed order, 1 to 21 (the lines 3207, 3208, 3209, 3210-3213, 3214, 3215-3219,
-- 3220-3223, 3224, 3225, 3226-3228, 3229, 3230, 3231, 3232, 3233, 3234, 3235, 3236-3238, 3239, 3240, 3241).  The label claims no official
-- number.  Counting the printed items (non-blank lines 3207-3241, with the continuation lines of an item joined to it) gives 21.
--
-- A TABLE.  Each item is one row: what is asked for, the kind of information (a number, a number and an amount, a copy, a description ...)
-- and whether it is asked of every supervisory authority or only of a self-regulatory organisation ("In the case of a self-regulatory
-- organisation, ...").  A row for an item that is asked only of a self-regulatory organisation answers NOTHING for another authority: the
-- item is limited by its own wording and says nothing of an authority that is not one.
--
-- WHAT THE ITEMS REFER TO.  "Regulation 26", "regulation 59", "regulation 60", "Part 8", "Part 9" and "regulation 104(4)" are provisions of
-- these Regulations that other parts encode; the Schedule names data to collect, and no answer crosses (PLAN.md, 5.5).  The Terrorism Act 2000
-- and the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 are not among the sources.  "Medium risk" (item 6(b)) has no constructor in the core's `Level of risk`
-- (which has `high risk`, `low risk` and `neither high nor low risk`), so this module declares its own `sch 4 risk rating` (NEEDS-CORE.md).

-- src:3206 | SCHEDULE 4 — Supervisory Information
§ `Schedule 4 -- Supervisory Information`

DECLARE `sch 4 kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 a number`
    `sch 4 a number and an amount`
    `sch 4 a number, an amount and a type`
    `sch 4 a copy`
    `sch 4 a description`
    `sch 4 an indication`
    `sch 4 an amount of human resource`

DECLARE `sch 4 of whom the item is asked` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 every supervisory authority`
    `sch 4 a self-regulatory organisation only`

-- Item 6: the three ratings of firms.
DECLARE `sch 4 risk rating` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 high risk`
    `sch 4 medium risk`
    `sch 4 low risk`

DECLARE `sch 4 item` HAS
    `the position of the item in the printed order`   IS A NUMBER
    `what the item asks for`                          IS A STRING
    `the kind of information`                         IS A `sch 4 kind of information`
    `of whom the item is asked`                       IS A `sch 4 of whom the item is asked`
    `the limbs of the item`                           IS A LIST OF STRING

-- src:3207 | The number of persons subject to the supervision of the supervisory authority, or in the case of a self-regulatory organisation, the number of its members (“supervised persons”).
@ref sch 4 item 1 (src:3207)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 1` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 1
        `what the item asks for` IS "the number of persons subject to the supervision of the supervisory authority, or in the case of a self-regulatory organisation, the number of its members"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a number`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 every supervisory authority`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST

-- "(“supervised persons”)" names the persons counted in item 1: those subject to the supervision of the authority, or, for a self-regulatory
-- organisation, its members.  The text does not use "means", so a person outside it is not said not to be one.
@ref sch 4 item 1 (src:3207)
GIVEN `the person is subject to the supervision of the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 item 1 the person is a supervised person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (NOT `the supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation`)
           AND `the person is subject to the supervision of the supervisory authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation`
           AND `the person is a member of the self-regulatory organisation`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "supervised persons" labels the persons the item counts; the text does not say that another person is not a supervised person

-- src:3208 | The number of supervised persons who are individuals.
@ref sch 4 item 2 (src:3208)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 2` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 2
        `what the item asks for` IS "the number of supervised persons who are individuals"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a number`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 every supervisory authority`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST


-- src:3209 | In the case of a self-regulatory organisation, the number of its supervised persons who act as trust or company service providers.
@ref sch 4 item 3 (src:3209)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 3` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 3
        `what the item asks for` IS "in the case of a self-regulatory organisation, the number of its supervised persons who act as trust or company service providers"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a number`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 a self-regulatory organisation only`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST


-- src:3210 | In the case of a self-regulatory organisation, the number of applications for membership which the organisation has—
-- src:3211 | (a) received,
-- src:3212 | (b) rejected, and
-- src:3213 | (c) accepted.
@ref sch 4 item 4 (src:3210-3213)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 4` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 4
        `what the item asks for` IS "in the case of a self-regulatory organisation, the number of applications for membership which the organisation has received, rejected and accepted"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a number`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 a self-regulatory organisation only`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST
            "received"
          , "rejected"
          , "accepted"


-- src:3214 | The services provided by supervised persons.
@ref sch 4 item 5 (src:3214)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 5` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 5
        `what the item asks for` IS "the services provided by supervised persons"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a description`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 every supervisory authority`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST


-- src:3215 | The number of firms subject to the supervision of the supervisory authority which the authority considers to be—
-- src:3216 | (a) high risk;
-- src:3217 | (b) medium risk;
-- src:3218 | (c) low risk;
-- src:3219 | and for these purposes, “risk” refers to the risk that the firm will be subject to money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref sch 4 item 6 (src:3215-3219)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 6` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 6
        `what the item asks for` IS "the number of firms subject to the supervision of the supervisory authority which the authority considers to be high risk, medium risk and low risk"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a number`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 every supervisory authority`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST
            "high risk"
          , "medium risk"
          , "low risk"

-- Item 6 counts firms by the authority's rating; the lettering (a), (b), (c) is the order high, medium, low.
@ref sch 4 item 6 (src:3215-3219)
GIVEN rating IS A `sch 4 risk rating`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 4 item 6 the limb that counts firms of that rating` MEANS
    CONSIDER rating
    WHEN `sch 4 high risk` THEN "(a)"
    WHEN `sch 4 medium risk` THEN "(b)"
    WHEN `sch 4 low risk` THEN "(c)"

-- "and for these purposes, 'risk' refers to the risk that the firm will be subject to money laundering or terrorist financing".
@ref sch 4 item 6 (src:3219)
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 4 item 6 risk refers to` MEANS "the risk that the firm will be subject to money laundering or terrorist financing"

-- src:3220 | The number of applications for approval received by the supervisory authority under regulation 26, and the number of those that—
-- src:3221 | (a) were refused;
-- src:3222 | (b) were accepted;
-- src:3223 | (c) are to be determined.
@ref sch 4 item 7 (src:3220-3223)
GIVETH A `sch 4 item`
`sch 4 item 7` MEANS
    `sch 4 item` WITH
        `the position of the item in the printed order` IS 7
        `what the item asks for` IS "the number of applications for approval received under regulation 26, and the number of those that were refused, were accepted and are to be determined"
        `the kind of information` IS `sch 4 a number`
        `of whom the item is asked` IS `sch 4 every supervisory authority`
        `the limbs of the item` IS LIST
            "were refused"
          , "were accepted"
          , "are to be determined"


-- src:3224 | The number of approvals under regulation 26 which were not valid, or ceased to be valid under paragraph (9) of that regulation.
@ref sch 4 item 8 (src:3224)
